==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|kirche}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|chirihha}}, an early borrowing from {{etyl|grc|de}} {{m|grc|κυριακόν}}. Compare Dutch {{m|nl|kerk}}, English {{m|en|church}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈkɪʁçə/|[ˈkɪʁçə]|[ˈkɪɐ̯çə]|lang=de}} {{a|standard}}
:* {{IPA|[ˈkɪɐ̯xə]|lang=de}} {{a|some speakers in southern Germany, Austria, and Switzerland}}
:* {{IPA|[ˈkiːɐ̯çə]|lang=de}} {{a|Westphalian}}
* {{audio|De-Kirche.ogg|audio (Germany)|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-at-Kirche.ogg|audio (Austria)|lang=de}}

